<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Reflected XSS</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/levels.css"></head>
<body><main class="wrap">
  <a href="/">← Lab home</a><p class="eyebrow">REFLECTED XSS</p><div class="level-badge <%= level %>"><%= level %> level</div><h1>Reflected XSS</h1>
  <nav class="level-nav" aria-label="Reflected XSS difficulty levels">
    <a class="<%= level === 'easy' ? 'selected' : '' %>" href="/reflected?level=easy">Easy</a>
    <a class="<%= level === 'medium' ? 'selected' : '' %>" href="/reflected?level=medium">Medium</a>
    <a class="<%= level === 'hard' ? 'selected' : '' %>" href="/reflected?level=hard">Hard</a>
  </nav>
  <% if (level === "easy") { %>
    <p><strong>Objective:</strong> trace a query parameter reflected directly into an HTML body.</p>
  <% } else if (level === "medium") { %>
    <p><strong>Objective:</strong> inspect how a query parameter is inserted into a quoted HTML attribute.</p>
  <% } else { %>
    <p><strong>Objective:</strong> trace a query parameter into a JavaScript string in the response.</p>
  <% } %>
  <form method="GET" action="/reflected"><input type="hidden" name="level" value="<%= level %>"><label for="q">Search term</label><input id="q" name="q" value="<%= q %>" placeholder="Try hello"><button>Search</button></form>
  <section class="result"><h2>Search result</h2>
    <% if (level === "easy") { %>
      <div class="unsafe-output"><%- q %></div>
    <% } else if (level === "medium") { %>
      <div class="unsafe-output" data-search="<%- q %>"><%= q %></div>
    <% } else { %>
      <div id="hard-output" class="unsafe-output">Search term is assigned from the response script.</div>
      <script>document.getElementById("hard-output").textContent = '<%- q %>';</script>
    <% } %>
  </section>
  <details><summary>Learning notes</summary><p>Each level uses an intentionally unsafe output context. Compare HTML body, HTML attribute, and JavaScript string contexts, then explain how each should be safely handled. Use harmless proof-of-execution payloads only.</p></details>
</main></body></html>